  "title": "The Giants' Wall | A Basque Legend | Full Fantasy Film",
  "description": "A work of fiction. All people and animals in this film are AI-generated. No real animals were harmed.<br><br>The Basque mountains, autumn 1862. Every dawn, the broken wall of Amaia Iturri&apos;s sheep fold has grown by exactly three great stones: stones no man could lift, a sprig with three acorns tucked between them, and bare footprints twice the length of a man&apos;s leading away into the fog.<br><br>Her grandfather Joanes knows who has come back after sixty years. In the old oak wood above the village, Amaia finds Handia, an old giant with a braided grey beard who mends walls and plants acorns. But Gaspar Ugalde, the ironmaster at the mouth of the valley, needs charcoal for his forge, and the only oaks left are the ones that hold up the mountain. When the autumn rains come, the whole valley learns what the giants&apos; walls were for.<br><br>The Giants&apos; Wall is an original cinematic story inspired by the Jentilak, the giants of Basque mythology. In the old stories, they raised the great stones of the mountains, then walked away and left the valleys to people.<br><br>Chapters<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kKyxvpnKnHw\">0:00</a> Prologue<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kKyxvpnKnHw&amp;t=68\">1:08</a> Chapter One: The Stones<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kKyxvpnKnHw&amp;t=517\">8:37</a> Chapter Two: The Acorns<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kKyxvpnKnHw&amp;t=955\">15:55</a> Chapter Three: The Charcoal<br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kKyxvpnKnHw&amp;t=1460\">24:20</a> Chapter Four: The Rain<br><br>Written &amp; directed by Gilded Myth Pictures<br>Cast: Amaia Iturri, a shepherdess · Joanes Iturri, her grandfather · Gaspar Ugalde, the ironmaster · Xabier Ugalde, his son · Handia, a giant of the oak wood<br>Music: YouTube Audio Library<br><br><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/mythology\">#mythology</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/fantasyfilm\">#fantasyfilm</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/legend\">#legend</a>",
